      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "### Problem\n\nAfter commit 4fb3b57a19cb83a99d4c5489982c22d96e28e8c2 some keys (for example Tab and Backspace) are being repeated. For example in normal mode, when deleting work using backspace two alphabets are being deleted.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nbuild vim from master (after 4fb3b57a19cb83a99d4c5489982c22d96e28e8c2)\nType in some sentences, insert normal mode, try deleting using backspace.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nKeys are not repeated (or only one alphabet is removed deleted when using backspace)\n\nAs it used to be before commit 4fb3b57a19cb83a99d4c5489982c22d96e28e8c2 was merged.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.11.0-dev-1444+g4fb3b57a19\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty 0.14.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nFrom git",
